gy, Yale University School of Medicine, New Haven, CT, 06511, USA. jean-leon.thomas@yale.edu."}]}}]}, "authorIdList": {"authorId": [{"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0001-5448-5865"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0001-7761-1684"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-3943-2850"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-5772-5999"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-2642-4402"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-3173-1474"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-3318-4697"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-4767-0442"}]}, "dataLinksTagsList": {"dataLinkstag": ["altmetrics", "supporting_data", "full_text", "related_data"]}, "journalInfo": {"issue": "1", "volume": "10", "journalIssueId": 2866016, "dateOfPublication": "2019 Oct", "monthOfPublication": 10, "yearOfPublication": 2019, "journal": {"medlineAbbreviation": "Nat Commun", "title": "Nature communications", "essn": "2041-1723", "issn": "2041-1723", "nlmid": "101528555", "isoabbreviation": "Nat Commun"}, "printPublicationDate": "2019-10-01"}, "pubYear": "2019", "pageInfo": "4594", "abstractText": "Cranial lymphatic vessels (LVs) are involved in the transport of fluids, macromolecules and central nervous system (CNS) immune responses. Little information about spinal LVs is available, because these delicate structures are embedded within vertebral tissues and difficult to visualize using traditional histology. Here we show an extended vertebral column LV network using three-dimensional imaging of decalcified iDISCO<sup>+</sup>-clarified spine segments. Vertebral LVs connect to peripheral sensory and sympathetic ganglia and form metameric vertebral circuits connecting to lymph nodes and the thoracic duct. They drain the epidural space and the dura mater around the spinal cord and associate with leukocytes. Vertebral LVs remodel extensively after spinal cord injury and VEGF-C-induced vertebral lymphangiogenesis exacerbates the inflammatory responses, T cell infiltration and demyelination following focal spinal cord lesion. Therefore, vertebral LVs add to skull meningeal LVs as gatekeepers of CNS immunity and may be potential targets to improve the maintenance and repair of spinal tissues.", "affiliation": "Université Pierre et Marie Curie Paris 06 UMRS1127, Sorbonne Université, Institut du Cerveau et de la Moelle Epinière, Paris, France.", "publicationStatus": "epublish", "language": "eng", "pubModel": "Electronic", "pubTypeList": {"pubType": ["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't", "research-article", "Journal Article", "Research Support, N.I.H., Extramural"]}, "grantsList": {"grant": [{"agency": "Cancer Foundation Finland sr", "grantId": "170102", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NEI NIH HHS", "acronym": "EY", "grantId": "P30 EY026878", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NIGMS NIH HHS", "acronym": "GM", "grantId": "T32 GM007205", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NCI NIH HHS", "acronym": "CA", "grantId": "F30 CA239444", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NEI NIH HHS", "acronym": "EY", "grantId": "R01 EY025979", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NHLBI NIH HHS", "acronym": "HL", "grantId": "R01 HL125811", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "European Research Council", "grantId": "743155", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NIBIB NIH HHS", "acronym": "EB", "grantId": "R01 EB016629", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NIDDK NIH HHS", "acronym": "DK", "grantId": "R01 DK120373", "orderIn": 0}]}, "meshHeadingList": {"meshHeading": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Spine", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "AH", "qualifierName": "anatomy & histology"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "abbreviation": "PH", "qualifierName": "physiology"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Lymph Nodes", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "AH", "qualifierName": "anatomy & histology"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "abbreviation": "PH", "qualifierName": "physiology"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Lymphatic Vessels", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualif